<title>JAPAN: Citizen Elec -6mth parent results.</title>
<headline>Citizen Elec -6mth parent results.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p> (Parent)	(in billions of yen unless specified)</p>
<p> Sales		 15.56		vs	   14.02</p>
<p> Operating	    1.44		vs	    1.06</p>
<p> Current		1.40		vs	    1.06</p>
<p> Net		  643    million	  vs	  421    million</p>
<p> EPS		   91.42 yen	  vs	  719.47 yen</p>
<p> Shares		7 million	  vs	 586,000</p>
<p> Interim div	  5.00 yen	  vs	   50.00 yen</p>
<p>NOTE - Citizen Electronics Co Ltd implemented 1:1.2</p>
<p>share split on March 22, 1996. And the compnay</p>
<p>also changed its share's face value from 500 yen</p>
<p>to 50 yen on July 31, 1996.</p>
</text>
